<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neustrelitz</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neustrelitz is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecklenburg-vorpommern">Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, founded in 1733 by Duke Adolphus Frederick III as the new residence of the dukes of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>. Laid out as a baroque planned town with streets radiating from a central market square, it remained the capital of Mecklenburg-Strelitz until the state merged with Mecklenburg-Schwerin in 1934.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neustrelitz.jpg" alt="Neustrelitz" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harke · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marktplatz_Neustrelitz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
